id "1ae2d51a-25d1-5c8a-8850-73da7e9a4e56" :question/math-academy-id "q-112615" :question/problem "Find the polynomial $P(x)$ given that\n\n$$\n3{x}^{4}-13{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+17x-6=(x-3)(x+1)P(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-13{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+17x-6.$ We know that $(x-3)$ and $(x+1)$ are factors of $f(x),$ and we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause $(x-3)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ we know that $(x-3)$ divides $f(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-3)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | ${x}^{4}$ | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $3$ | $-13$ | $7$ | $17$ | $-6$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $9$ | $-12$ | $-15$ | $6$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-4$ | $-5$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{4}-13{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+17x-6}{x-3}=3{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-5x+2,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n3{x}^{4}-13{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+17x-6=(x-3)(3{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-5x+2).\n$$\n\nNow, because $(x+1)$ is also a factor of $f(x),$ it must be a factor of the quotient $(3{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-5x+2).$ So, we divide this quotient by $(x+1)$ using synthetic division once more:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $-5$ | $2$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-3$ | $7$ | $-2$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-7$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-5x+2}{x+1}=3{x}^{2}-7x+2,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n3{x}^{4}-13{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+17x-6=(x-3)(x+1)(3{x}^{2}-7x+2).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n3{x}^{4}-13{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}+17x-6=(x-3)(x+1){{(3x-1)(x-2)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=(3x-1)(x-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112615/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e897cc-b3fe-5d2f-8b47-3afdfe276bcf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112615"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-18862/selection/bb6a39521e96c29467f9fe09a15afc8fb624cce4b2b710ae0937e90cbf138778" :answer/id #uuid "4becc13b-bd42-5cb3-a0ef-f0792c79cfc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)(x-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18862/selection/504c86cc017232e1994848668eb33854581534fcfab70f59f76f8e3432e63c64" :answer/id #uuid "144357e3-9b78-5cc9-9951-bdf3d8766319" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18862/selection/621024d70f5fd48e0e736dc0116fc3c72f8cd6d078a026dbd74de294432bd5bc" :answer/id #uuid "3387aec4-d932-595f-b00b-04bff128f3a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1-x)(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18862/selection/8dd10df374f0623ba54c634fa4554f2f28b49deaf043daa63d03fe13c2379e05" :answer/id #uuid "101975c3-dba1-5282-8121-9e60613858f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)(x-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18862/selection/d4c887d0bdccfdcf0fbf9340b6396bd14fe442a76950895fd4942dfe929451de" :answer/id #uuid "06417c26-3c72-5e2c-90cf-78759f2cb038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-18862/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d48e852f-4f2f-54bd-9210-e9bff195a1be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-18862/selection/504c86cc017232e1994848668eb33854581534fcfab70f59f76f8e3432e63c64" :answer-field/choices ["q-18862/selection/bb6a39521e96c29467f9fe09a15afc8fb624cce4b2b710ae0937e90cbf138778" "q-18862/selection/504c86cc017232e1994848668eb33854581534fcfab70f59f76f8e3432e63c64" "q-18862/selection/621024d70f5fd48e0e736dc0116fc3c72f8cd6d078a026dbd74de294432bd5bc" "q-18862/selection/8dd10df374f0623ba54c634fa4554f2f28b49deaf043daa63d03fe13c2379e05" "q-18862/selection/d4c887d0bdccfdcf0fbf9340b6396bd14fe442a76950895fd4942dfe929451de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-18862" :question/id #uuid "a2347a20-a04a-5345-8cd6-614ad9c964ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-18862" :question/problem "Find the polynomial $P(x)$ given that \n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-11{x}^{2}+9x+18=(x-2)(x-3)P(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-11{x}^{2}+9x+18.$ We know that $(x-2)$ and $(x-3)$ are factors of $f(x),$ and we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause $(x-3)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ we know that $(x-3)$ divides $f(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-3)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | ${x}^{4}$ | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-11$ | $9$ | $18$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $3$ | $6$ | $-15$ | $-18$ |\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $-5$ | $-6$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-11{x}^{2}+9x+18}{x-3}={x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-5x-6,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-11{x}^{2}+9x+18=(x-3)({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-5x-6).\n$$\n\nNow, because $(x-2)$ is also a factor of $f(x),$ it must be a factor of the quotient $({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-5x-6).$ So, we divide this quotient by $(x-2)$ using synthetic division once more:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-5$ | $-6$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $2$ | $8$ | $6$ |\n|  | $1$ | $4$ | $3$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-5x-6}{x-2}={x}^{2}+4x+3,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-11{x}^{2}+9x+18=(x-2)(x-3)({x}^{2}+4x+3).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-11{x}^{2}+9x+18=(x-2)(x-3){{(x+1)(x+3)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=(x+1)(x+3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-18862/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e897cc-b3fe-5d2f-8b47-3afdfe276bcf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18862"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112617/selection/5811371a8859c22a0423954b4290808ad371c5d047ab4ce4ed9235486fffaf4