blem "Find the polynomial $P(x)$ given that\n\n$$\n3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-37{x}^{2}-14x+24=(x-3)(x+4)P(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-37{x}^{2}-14x+24.$ We know that $(x-3)$ and $(x+4)$ are factors of $f(x),$ and we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause $(x-3)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ we know that $(x-3)$ divides $f(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-3)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | ${x}^{4}$ | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $3$ | $4$ | $-37$ | $-14$ | $24$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $9$ | $39$ | $6$ | $-24$ |\n|  | $3$ | $13$ | $2$ | $-8$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-37{x}^{2}-14x+24}{x-3}=3{x}^{3}+13{x}^{2}+2x-8,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-37{x}^{2}-14x+24=(x-3)(3{x}^{3}+13{x}^{2}+2x-8).\n$$\n\nNow, because $(x+4)$ is also a factor of $f(x),$ it must be a factor of the quotient $(3{x}^{3}+13{x}^{2}+2x-8).$ So, we divide this quotient by $(x+4)$ using synthetic division once more:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $3$ | $13$ | $2$ | $-8$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-12$ | $-4$ | $8$ |\n|  | $3$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}+13{x}^{2}+2x-8}{x+4}=3{x}^{2}+x-2,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-37{x}^{2}-14x+24=(x-3)(x+4)(3{x}^{2}+x-2).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n3{x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-37{x}^{2}-14x+24=(x-3)(x+4){{(3x-2)(x+1)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=(3x-2)(x+1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-112617/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e897cc-b3fe-5d2f-8b47-3afdfe276bcf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112617"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-328505/field-1/e2769b39988190e7ff0218723246f1ca450f53cc124b6a3fa5b88a357814cce9" :answer/id #uuid "812ffc62-3765-508e-93e5-6201ecaba3df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x^2+x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328505/field-1/1f6c604598f91512181771f825aa302c7882b6fddfd929fbe21756af91c0e821" :answer/id #uuid "590472f9-02b3-566f-9f21-f3dd5247618f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x^2+x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-328505/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "31f36e25-b61f-5321-ad42-f00f24ae5587" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-328505/field-1/e2769b39988190e7ff0218723246f1ca450f53cc124b6a3fa5b88a357814cce9" :answer-field/choices ["q-328505/field-1/e2769b39988190e7ff0218723246f1ca450f53cc124b6a3fa5b88a357814cce9" "q-328505/field-1/1f6c604598f91512181771f825aa302c7882b6fddfd929fbe21756af91c0e821"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-328505" :question/id #uuid "4a62cf7f-46f6-57be-87c1-f3c7b68c20fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-328505" :question/problem "The polynomial \n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+16x-12\n$$\n\n \ncan be expressed as\n\n$$\n(x-2)(x-3)\\cdot P(x).\n$$\n\nFind the polynomial $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+16x-12.$ We know that $(x-2)$ and $(x-3)$ are factors of $f(x),$ and we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause $(x-2)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ we know that $(x-2)$ divides $f(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-2)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | ${x}^{4}$ | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $1$ | $-4$ | $-1$ | $16$ | $-12$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $2$ | $-4$ | $-10$ | $12$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-2$ | $-5$ | $6$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+16x-12}{x-2}={x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-5x+6,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+16x-12=(x-2)({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-5x+6).\n$$\n\nNow, because $(x-3)$ is also a factor of $f(x),$ it must be a factor of the quotient $({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-5x+6).$ So, we divide this quotient by $(x-3)$ using synthetic division once more:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $-5$ | $6$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $3$ | $3$ | $-6$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}-5x+6}{x-3}={x}^{2}+x-2,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+16x-12=(x-2)(x-3)({x}^{2}+x-2).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(x)={x}^{2}+x-2=(x+2)(x-1).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328505/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e897cc-b3fe-5d2f-8b47-3afdfe276bcf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328505"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112626/selection/8257f359b8157975553fcd10e4617600a61318dbe0a39df31bd1db786e557703" :answer/id #uuid "b9e1f894-5119-59cc-bfdb-c9183dd9bfe5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2-x)(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112626/selection/2f574c49313afd1be00c55b430dd7e1a6e5d9efe12bd1b3005173a035ff529f0" :answer/id #uuid "0442d2db-b533-52e6-866e-1639306f629a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-5)(x+7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112626/selection/0e354034420aee1fdb5240bac9e4884030e2ee7bd6cdfa31299fdc7e584146a9" :answer/id #uuid "c4fd975c-47c6-555c-b100-82be99870988" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)(x+7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112626/selection/501c1a6f2d5e8d79e9f013a7ee133c1d101f4f088ec8a6e463b1332dd1669d3e" :answer/id #uuid "49932a8b-4c10-59c7-b96f-8242e9717c7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-7)(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112626/selection/d503c05612d35fda63080e4a042f35b2da43780f319372112eeb639a7f60497e" :answer/id #uuid "8919c6de-f31e-5255-96ce-2366c5618d98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)(5-x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112626/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1cb3d32b-bf2f-524a-9749-7a9953bc7e94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112626/selection/0e354034420aee1fdb5240bac9e4884030e2ee7bd6cdfa31299fdc7e584146a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-112626/selection/8257f359b8157975553fcd10e4617600a61318dbe0a39df31bd1db786e557703" "q-112626/selection/2f574c49313afd1be00c55b430dd7e1a6e5d9efe12bd1b3005173a035ff529f0" "q-112626/selection/0e354034420aee1fdb5240bac9e4884030e2ee7bd6cdfa31299fdc7e584146a9" "q-112626/selection/501c1a6f2d5e8d79e9f013a7ee133c1d101f4f088ec8a6e463b1332dd1669d3e" "q-112626/selection/d503c05612d35fda63080e4a042f35b2da43780f319372112eeb639a7f60497e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112626" :question/id #uuid "b141ec1c-c50d-54e9-aeb4-343e8225692d" :question/math-academy-id "q-112626" :question/problem "Find the polynomial $P(x)$ given that \n\n$$\n{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-2x+35=(x-5)(x+1)P(x).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-2x+35.$ We know that $(x-5)$ and $(x+1)$ are factors of $f(x),$ and we need to find its other factors.\n\nBecause $(x-5)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ we know that $(x-5)$ divides $f(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-5)$ using synthetic division:\n\n\\\n\n|  | ${x}^{4}$ | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-36$ | $-2$ | $35$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $5$ | $35$ | $-5$ | $-35$ |\n|  | $1$ | $7$ | $-1$ | $-7$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-2x+35}{x-5}={x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-x-7,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-2x+35=(x-5)({x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-x-7).\n$$\n\nNow, because $(x+1)$ is also a factor of $f(x),$ it must be a factor of the quotient $({x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-x-7).$ So, we divide this quotient by $(x+1)$ using synthetic division once more:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $7$ | $-1$ | $-7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $-6$ | $7$ |\n|  | $1$ | $6$ | $-7$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-x-7}{x+1}={x}^{2}+6x-7,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-2x+35=(x-5)(x+1)({x}^{2}+6x-7).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-2x+35=(x-5)(x+1){{(x-1)(x+7)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=(x-1)(x+7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-112626/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e897cc-b3fe-5d2f-8b47-3afdfe276bcf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112626"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-112638/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "8907e2af-8a8e-50d4-ab9b-465238830ee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112638/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "cfa410a5-e84d-54ba-9770-805c995a6c1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112638/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "dfb03cab-6129-57e4-9296-9bbe9a7d8f9c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112638/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "2bc6c00a-5061-5c3c-9929-85279736e5d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112638/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "ef5c14b0-9de1-5c5a-a77f-2ed6e6ef3822" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-112638/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e928d599-81a6-5751-a391-da81fd0fc2b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-112638/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-112638/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-112638/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-112638/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-112638/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-112638/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-112638" :question/id #uuid "9075ffae-791a-5f2a-9a0d-309b380c2bd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-112638" :question/problem "Let $p(x)={x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-35{x}^{2}-57x+90.$ Given that $p(-3)=p(1)=0,$ find the sum of all distinct real roots of $p(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $p(-3)=p(1)=0,$ by factor theorem $(x+3)$ and $(x-1)$ are both factors of $p(x).$\nTo factor $p(x)$ completely we need to find its other factors.\n\nSince $(x-1)$ is a factor of $p(x),$ we know that $(x-1)$ divides $p(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $p(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-1)$ using synthetic division:\n\n|  | ${x}^{4}$ | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $1$ | $-35$ | $-57$ | $90$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-33$ | $-90$ |\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $-33$ | $-90$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-35{x}^{2}-57x+90}{x-1}={x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-33x-90,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-35{x}^{2}-57x+90=(x-1)({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-33x-90).\n$$\n\nNow, because $(x+3)$ is also a factor of $p(x),$ it must be a factor of the quotient $({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-33x-90).$ So, we divide this quotient by $(x+3)$ using synthetic division once more:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-33$ | $-90$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-3$ | $3$ | $90$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-1$ | $-30$ | $0$ |\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-33x-90}{x+3}={x}^{2}-x-30,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-35{x}^{2}-57x+90=(x-1)(x+3)({x}^{2}-x-30).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-35{x}^{2}-57x+90=(x-1)(x+3)(x-6)(x+5).\n$$\n\nWe can now equate each factor to zero and solve for $x$ to find the three roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =1\\,,\\,x=-3\\,,\\,x=6\\,,\\,x=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the sum of the roots of the polynomial is\n\n$$\n1-3+6-5=-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-112638/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98c87ea4-2431-5088-8717-815efd1403ff"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-112638"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-270967/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "28a566b8-7707-5ebe-8ec0-d3f60d5e3a51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-270967/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "8486ff9e-14c6-5eb2-b3b9-4faf3d8d5640" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-270967/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d1946d2-8237-555e-95dd-11d303acade5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-270967/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-270967/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-270967/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-270967/field-2/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "2c23790a-7470-5758-